  "body_html": "<p dir=\"auto\">A similar question was asked before but without a resolution. I want to get the connection state after I called HtmlWebSocketChannel.connect.<br>\nThe reason is hat I want to display a successful connection in the statusbar and add the Url to a history list. Right now I can only get a callback if the connection failed. But that would only happen asynchronously after I connect.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"channel = HtmlWebSocketChannel.connect('ws://' + url);\nchannel.stream.listen(\n  _receiveMessage,\n  onError: (e) {\n    print('Could not connect to: $url');\n  },\n  onDone: () {\n    print('Connection closed');\n  },\n);\nupdate_statusbar(url);  // FIXME: here I do not know if the connection was successful or not!\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">channel = HtmlWebSocketChannel.connect('ws://' + url);\nchannel.stream.listen(\n  _receiveMessage,\n  onError: (e) {\n    print('Could not connect to: $url');\n  },\n  onDone: () {\n    print('Connection closed');\n  },\n);\nupdate_statusbar(url);  // FIXME: here I do not know if the connection was successful or not!\n</code></pre></div>",
  "body_text": "A similar question was asked before but without a resolution. I want to get the connection state after I called HtmlWebSocketChannel.connect.\nThe reason is hat I want to display a successful connection in the statusbar and add the Url to a history list. Right now I can only get a callback if the connection failed. But that would only happen asynchronously after I connect.\nchannel = HtmlWebSocketChannel.connect('ws://' + url);\nchannel.stream.listen(\n  _receiveMessage,\n  onError: (e) {\n    print('Could not connect to: $url');\n  },\n  onDone: () {\n    print('Connection closed');\n  },\n);\nupdate_statusbar(url);  // FIXME: here I do not know if the connection was successful or not!",
